From f089aacdffa86d6064bb7d095376410ce04f82f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:54:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] quantize: nudge scalefactors by one step to make the deltas
 cheaper to code

Each coded band may move its scalefactor one step either way. A Viterbi pass
over the coded bands of a group picks the moves that minimize the Huffman
bits of the scalefactor deltas (plus a quarter bit per step moved). Costs are
integers, so the choice cannot differ between platforms. Stereo LC at a set
rate only, like the masking target.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GANKWjRgBdQpP7qFdY92JS
---
 libfaac/frame.c    |   4 ++
 libfaac/quantize.c | 116 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 libfaac/quantize.h |   1 +
 3 files changed, 107 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

